Short:        Shows equivalents for number systems.
Author:       Eric S. Raymond
Uploader:     amimjf connectfree com (Matthew J Fletcher)
Type:         dev/c
Version:      2.7
Replaces:     -
Requires:     ixemul v48+
Architecture: m68k-amigaos
Distribution: Aminet


This is a handy little utility that recognizes many different ways of
naming an ASCII character (hex, octal, binary, decimal, C escape, ISO
character table pair, slang names, and others) and prints out all the
equivalents.

The latest sources at http://www.tuxedo.org/~esr/ascii/

                            Eric S. Raymond
                            esr@thyrsus.com


AmigaOS Notes.
egcs wont compile it under libnix, so you will need ixemul v48+ to use it.
You can get this from aminet, you also get a sensible text file rarther
than a man page, buts its still unix syntax, but its about time you learned
it anyway.


